{"id": "section-body-13210", "title": "Anaphylaxis", "chapterId": "chapter-thirteen", "blocks": [{"id": "body-13210", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading2", "text": "Anaphylaxis", "runs": [{"text": "Anaphylaxis"}], "level": 2, "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1368"}}, {"id": "body-13211", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "It is an acute and often life-threatening immunologic reaction, frequently heralded by scalp pruritus, diffuse erythema, urticaria, or angioedema. Bronchospasm, laryngeal edema, hyperperistalsis, hypotension, and cardiac arrhythmia may occur. Antibiotics (especially penicillin), other drugs, and radiographic contrast agents are the most common causes of serious anaphylactic reactions.", "runs": [{"text": "It"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "an"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "acute"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "often"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "life-threatening"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "immunologic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "reaction,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "frequently"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "heralded"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "by"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "scalp"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "pruritus,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "diffuse"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "erythema,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "urticaria, or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "angioedema."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Bronchospasm,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "laryngeal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "edema,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "hyperperistalsis,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "hypotension,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cardiac"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "arrhythmia"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "may"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "occur."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Antibiotics (especially penicillin), other drugs, and radiographic contrast agents are the most common causes of serious anaphylactic "}, {"text": "reactions."}]}, {"id": "body-13213", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Management: Refer to chapter on approach to patients with emergency conditions", "runs": [{"text": "Management:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "Refer"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "chapter"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "on"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "approach"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "patients"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "emergency"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "conditions"}]}], "source": {"file": "medical.docx", "chapter": "Skin diseases", "start": "body-13210", "end": "body-13213"}}